# Event Service walkthrough (events, RSVPs, check-in, files) for api/event.py.
# Select the REST Client environment, then send each numbered request top to bottom,
# checking the expected status in its heading. The uid and password are prompts; never
# write them into this file. Creates real rows in the selected environment: one event at
# @pagePath, your RSVP and check-in, a photo and a video link. Run it once per database:
# the event ends archived, which is read only (removing a file is the one change left).
@pagePath = /events/events-demo/

### 1. Authenticate as a Teacher or Admin (expect 200)
# @name login
# @prompt uid Enter a Teacher or Admin user ID
# @prompt password Enter your password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{uid}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. The options a page checks an event with: statuses and moves, roles, file kinds, limits with first_year and last_year (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event/options
Accept: application/json

### 3. The list of public events, by start (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event
Accept: application/json

### 4. Create the event with the event front matter keys (pages#2089), as a draft (expect 201; 409 with the existing id if it already exists)
# @name createEvent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "page_path": "{{pagePath}}",
  "title": "Community Technology Workshop (demo)",
  "description": "An introduction to practical AI.",
  "date": "2027-03-15",
  "start_time": "10:00",
  "end_time": "13:00",
  "timezone": "America/Los_Angeles",
  "categories": ["Community", "Technology", "Workshop"],
  "event_type": "workshop",
  "location": {"name": "Community Center", "address": "Poway, California"},
  "organizer": {"name": "Open Coding Society"},
  "registration": {"enabled": true, "capacity": 50},
  "attachments": [{"type": "gallery", "id": "workshop-gallery"}, {"type": "document", "id": "workshop-agenda"}],
  "features": {"microblog": true, "registration": true, "attendance": true, "gallery": true},
  "body": "## Agenda\n\nBring a laptop."
}

### 4b. A start time the clocks skip, 02:30 on 2027-03-14 in Los Angeles: refused, and nothing is made (expect 400, code "no_such_time", field "start_time")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "page_path": "/events/events-demo-clock-change/",
  "title": "Clock change (demo)",
  "date": "2027-03-14",
  "start_time": "02:30",
  "end_time": "04:00",
  "timezone": "America/Los_Angeles"
}

### 5. Read it by its page: a draft, which only its managers see, and it can move only to published (expect 200, viewer.next_statuses ["published"])
# @name event
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event?page_path={{pagePath}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Open registration straight from draft: refused, and allowed lists where it can go (expect 409, code "transition")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/status
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "status": "registration"
}

### 7. Publish it (expect 200, status "published" and published_at set)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/status
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "status": "published"
}

### 8. Set the organizer's notice, the banner at the top of the page (expect 200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "notice": "Doors open at 9:45"
}

### 9. Open registration (expect 200, status "registration")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/status
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "status": "registration"
}

### 10. RSVP (expect 200, rsvp "going")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/rsvp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}}
}

### 11. Cancel the RSVP (expect 200, rsvp "declined")
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/event/rsvp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}}
}

### 12. RSVP again (expect 200, rsvp "going")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/rsvp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}}
}

### 13. The check-in code before the event is active: refused (expect 409, code "not_open", action "check_in")
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event/checkin?event_id={{event.response.body.$.event.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 14. Start the event (expect 200, status "active")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/status
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "status": "active"
}

### 15. The check-in code for the screen, new every 5 minutes (expect 200)
# @name code
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event/checkin?event_id={{event.response.body.$.event.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 16. Check in with that code, as someone at the door would (expect 200, checked_in_at set)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event/checkin
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "code": "{{code.response.body.$.code}}"
}

### 17. Check in with a code that is not on the screen (expect 400, code "bad_code")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event/checkin
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "code": "AAAAAAAA"
}

### 18. The roster, for the event's managers (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event/participants?event_id={{event.response.body.$.event.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 19. Clear your own check-in, as an organizer would by name (expect 200, checked_in_at null)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/participants
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "uid": "{{login.response.body.$.user.uid}}",
  "checked_in": false
}

### 20. Add a tiny PNG to the gallery, with its alt text (expect 201)
# @name photo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event/files
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "group": "workshop-gallery",
  "kind": "gallery",
  "name": "dot.png",
  "content": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNkYAAAAAYAAjCB0C8AAAAASUVORK5CYII=",
  "alt": "A single dot, standing in for a photo of the workshop"
}

### 21. The file itself (expect 200, image/png, shown inline)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event/files?id={{photo.response.body.$.file.id}}

### 22. Change the photo's alt text (expect 200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/files
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{photo.response.body.$.file.id}},
  "alt": "A single dot on a white background"
}

### 23. Add a YouTube link to the gallery; only the link is kept (expect 201, with link and no url)
# @name video
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event/files
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "group": "workshop-gallery",
  "kind": "gallery",
  "name": "Workshop recording",
  "link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ"
}

### 23b. The same link again in the same group: refused (expect 409, code "link_taken")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event/files
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "group": "workshop-gallery",
  "kind": "gallery",
  "name": "Workshop recording",
  "link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ"
}

### 24a. Complete the event (expect 200, status "completed")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/status
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "status": "completed"
}

### 24b. Then archive it (expect 200, status "archived")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event/status
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "status": "archived"
}

### 25. Change an archived event: refused, it is read only (expect 409, code "not_open", action "edit")
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/event
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{event.response.body.$.event.id}},
  "title": "Changed after the event"
}

### 25b. Remove the video link from the archived event: a manager can always take a file down (expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/event/files
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": {{video.response.body.$.file.id}}
}

### 26. The events bundle a migration copies (expect 200 as an Admin; 403 for a Teacher)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/export/events
Accept: application/json
